anuary-evening-slot","topic":"chemical-equilibrium-law-of-mass-action-and-equilibrium-constant","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":[],"yearKey":"jee-main-2020-online-9th-january-evening-slot","active":true},{"country":"in","examGroup":"jee","exam":"jee-main","subjectGroup":null,"subject":"chemistry","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","chapter":"periodic-table-and-periodicity","year":2020,"paperTitle":"JEE Main 2020 (Online) 9th January Evening Slot","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"languages":["en"],"difficulty":"easy","topicName":null,"type":"mcq","examDate":"2020-01-09 14:30","question":{"en":{"content":"The first and second ionisation enthalpies of a\nmetal are 496 and 4560 kJ mol<sup>–1</sup>, respectively.\nHow many moles of HCl and H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub>,\nrespectively, will be needed to react completely\nwith 1 mole of the metal hydroxide ?","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"1 and 2"},{"identifier":"B","content":"1 and 0.5"},{"identifier":"C","content":"1 and 1"},{"identifier":"D","content":"2 and 0.5"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"First ionization enthalpies = 496 kJ/mole\n<br><br>Second ionization enthalpies = 4560 kJ/mol\n<br><br>According to the given information, the difference between first and second ionization enthalpy is very high so Metal belong to 1st group i.e. Monovalent cation.\n<br><br>Metal hydroxide will be of type, MOH.\n<br><br>MOH + HCl <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.181ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -511 1000 522\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> MCl + H<sub>2</sub>O\n<br><br>MOH + <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.781ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.795ex\" height=\"2.737ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -864.9 793.6 1209.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><rect width=\"553.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub>\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.181ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -511 1000 522\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.781ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.795ex\" height=\"2.737ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -864.9 793.6 1209.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><rect width=\"553.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>M<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub> + H<sub>2</sub>O\n<br><br>So one mole of HCl required to react with one\nmole MOH.\n<br><br>And <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.781ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.795ex\" height=\"2.737ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -864.9 793.6 1209.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><rect width=\"553.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> mole of H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub> required to react with one\nmole MOH."},"hi":{"content":"एक धातु के पहले और दूसरे आयनन ऊर्जा क्रमशः 496 और 4560 kJ mol<sup>–1</sup> हैं। 1 मोल धातु हाइड्रोक्साइड के साथ पूरी तरह से प्रतिक्रिया करने के लिए HCl और H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub> के कितने मोल की आवश्यकता होगी?","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"1 और 2"},{"identifier":"B","content":"1 और 0.5"},{"identifier":"C","content":"1 और 1"},{"identifier":"D","content":"2 और 0.5"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":null,"comprehension":null,"direction":null}},"question_id":"PNpMWKAgPnACxm6HWa7k9k2k5lfq2nr","updated_time":1579956720,"permalink":"the-first-and-second-ionisation-enthalpies-of-a-metal-are-49-jee-main-chemistry-periodic-table-and-periodicity